    "fileId": 31257,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "IgG4-related sialadenitis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Low-power magnification shows variable degrees of inflammation, glandular atrophy, and fibrosis in different areas of the submandibular gland. Note the accentuated lobular architecture (&lt;&lt;31257&gt;&gt;). Periductal lymphocytic and plasma cell infiltrate is present, and lymphoepithelial lesions are typically absent (&lt;&lt;31258&gt;&gt;). There is an atrophic area with storiform fibrosis and a few residual ducts (&lt;&lt;31259&gt;&gt;). IgG immunostaining shows IgG4+ plasma cells (left) constituting &gt;&nbsp;60% of all IgG+ plasma cells (right) (&lt;&lt;31260&gt;&gt;).",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/63/285/31257.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/63/285/thumb_31257.jpg"
